{"name":"Raging Bull","hex":"#b54e45","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raging","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of rage"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Volatile, very active or unpredictable.","In a state of rage; in a state of extreme, often uncontrollable, anger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raging"},{"term":"bull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male, specifically:\n An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen.","An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large and strong, like a bull.","Of large mammals, adult male."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raging Bull","blocks":[{"text":"Raging Bull is a 1980 American biographical sports drama film directed by Martin Scorsese from a screenplay by Paul Schrader and Mardik Martin, which adapts Jake LaMotta's 1970 memoir Raging Bull: My Story. Robert De Niro stars as LaMotta, a former middleweight boxing champion whose turbulent personal life is beset by rage and jealousy. Scorsese dedicated the film to Armenian-American NYU film professor Haig P. Manoogian. The supporting cast includes Joe Pesci, Cathy Moriarty, Theresa Saldana, Frank Vincent and Nicholas Colasanto in his final film role."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Raging_Bull_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raging_Bull","wikidata":"Q220780"},{"title":"Raging Bull (roller coaster)","blocks":[{"text":"Raging Bull is a steel roller coaster located at Six Flags Great America, an amusement park in Gurnee, Illinois, United States. The ride opened to the public on May 1, 1999, as the first hyper-twister roller coaster, the second Hyper Coaster model built by Bolliger & Mabillard, and the tallest and longest coaster in the park."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1e/Raging_Bull_Logo.svg/330px-Raging_Bull_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raging_Bull_(roller_coaster)","wikidata":"Q1536832"},{"title":"Bull","blocks":[{"text":"A bull is an intact adult male of the species Bos taurus (cattle). More muscular and aggressive than the females of the same species, bulls have long been an important symbol in many religions, including for sacrifices. These animals play a significant role in beef ranching, dairy farming, and a variety of sporting and cultural activities, including bullfighting and bull riding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg/330px-A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull","wikidata":"Q693690"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Jake_LaMotta_signed_photo_postcard_1952.JPG/500px-Jake_LaMotta_signed_photo_postcard_1952.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Jake_LaMotta_signed_photo_postcard_1952.JPG/500px-Jake_LaMotta_signed_photo_postcard_1952.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJake_LaMotta_signed_photo_postcard_1952.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/RobertdeNiro26_%28cropped2%29.JPG/500px-RobertdeNiro26_%28cropped2%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/RobertdeNiro26_%28cropped2%29.JPG/1280px-RobertdeNiro26_%28cropped2%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th